language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Place rectangular items with given widths and heights inside a larger rectangle without overlap and within its boundaries, minimising the area of the larger rectangle.
given heights_dim1 : int(1..)
letting n = heights_dim1
given heights : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(1..)
given widths : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(1..)
find pos_x : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..sum(widths))
find pos_y : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..sum(heights))
find total_x : int(max(widths)..sum(widths))
find total_y : int(max(heights)..sum(heights))

branching on [total_x, total_y, pos_x, pos_y]
heuristic sdf

minimising total_x * total_y

such that
$ the larger rectangle has at least the total area of the items
total_x * total_y >= sum i : int(1..n) . widths[i] * heights[i],
$ every item lies within the larger rectangle, horizontally and vertically
forAll i : int(1..n) . (pos_x[i] + widths[i] <= total_x),
forAll i : int(1..n) . (pos_y[i] + heights[i] <= total_y),
$ no two items overlap: one lies left of, right of, below or above the other
forAll i : int(1..n) . forAll j : int(i+1..n) . ((pos_x[i] + widths[i] <= pos_x[j]) \/ (pos_x[j] + widths[j] <= pos_x[i]) \/ (pos_y[i] + heights[i] <= pos_y[j]) \/ (pos_y[j] + heights[j] <= pos_y[i]))
